---
import Section from '../components/site/Section.astro';
import { pageAt } from '../data/pages.ts';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CONTRIBUTING_URL, REPO_URL, TECH_DESIGN_URL } from '../lib/links.ts';

const guides = [pageAt('/docs/install'), pageAt('/docs/compose'), pageAt('/self-hosting')];
---

<Page
  page={pageAt('/docs')}
  lede="Guides for running Bemmoly on your own server. They grow with each release; anything not covered yet is in the README and the technical design."
>
  <Section title="Run it">
    <dl class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      {guides.map((guide) => (
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
          <dt>
            <a href={guide.path} class="font-semibold">
              {guide.name}
            </a>
          </dt>
          <dd>{guide.description}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Look after it">
    <p>
      Once it is running, the <code>bemmoly</code> command on the server covers the day-to-day:
      <code>bemmoly status</code> and <code>bemmoly doctor</code> for health, then
      <code>bemmoly backup</code> and <code>bemmoly restore</code>, and then
      <code>bemmoly upgrade</code> and <code>bemmoly rollback</code>, each with a backup first. The{' '}
      <a href="/docs/install#after">install guide</a> lists them all.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Understand it">
    <p>
      The <a href={REPO_URL}>README</a> explains what Bemmoly is and what each release adds. The
      <a href={TECH_DESIGN_URL}>technical design</a> describes the architecture, the module system,
      the data model, the AI subsystem and how installs, updates and backups work.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Build on it">
    <p>
      <a href={CONTRIBUTING_URL}>Contributing</a> is the contract for changes to the code, whether
      made by a person or an agent.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Page>
